<title>USA: TWA waives advance purchase restrictions.</title>
<headline>TWA waives advance purchase restrictions.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc. said Friday it was waiving advance purchase, minimum stay and other restrictions for its discounted tickets for any passenger displaced by a possible strike at AMR Corp.'s American Airlines.</p>
<p>TWA said passengers with American Airlines tickets purchased before Feb. 15 can obtain a reservation on TWA, on the same city pair routing, and have discounted ticket restrictions waived.</p>
<p>The waiver is effective through March 1. All seats are subject to availability.</p>
<p>TWA said American Airlines Admiral's Club members also may use TWA's Ambassadors Clubs by presenting a TWA boarding pass and Admiral's Club card.</p>
</text>
